(3.1 The Cell Membrane) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The plasma membrane is defined as a selectively permeable barrier that surrounds the cell.) Tj
T*
(It is composed of a phospholipid bilayer in which proteins are embedded.) Tj
T*
(Because the bilayer is hydrophobic at its core, small nonpolar molecules cross it freely,) Tj
T*
(while ions and large polar molecules require transport proteins to pass through.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 43 0 R >> >> /Contents 10 0 R >>
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 482 >>
