BT
/F1 11 Tf
56 730 Td
14 TL
(Membrane Transport) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Passive transport is defined as movement of a substance across a membrane without energy input.) Tj
T*
(Diffusion is the net movement of particles from a region of higher concentration to lower concentration.) Tj
T*
(Osmosis is defined as the diffusion of water across a selectively permeable membrane.) Tj
T*
(Active transport, in contrast, requires ATP because it moves substances against their gradient.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
