/F1 11 Tf
56 730 Td
14 TL
(3.2 Organelles) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The nucleus is defined as the membrane-bound organelle that stores the cell's genetic material.) Tj
T*
(The nucleolus is a dense region inside the nucleus where ribosomes are assembled.) Tj
T*
(Mitochondria are organelles that generate most of the cell's ATP through cellular respiration.) Tj
T*
(Because mitochondria contain their own DNA, they are thought to have originated as bacteria.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
