56 730 Td
14 TL
(3.3 The Cell Cycle) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The cell cycle is defined as the ordered sequence of events that produces two daughter cells.) Tj
T*
(Interphase is the growth stage, divided into the G1, S and G2 phases.) Tj
T*
(DNA replication occurs during the S phase, so that each chromosome is duplicated before division.) Tj
T*
(Checkpoints halt the cycle when damage is detected, which prevents faulty cells from dividing.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 43 0 R >> >> /Contents 18 0 R >>
endobj
