stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
56 730 Td
14 TL
(Mitosis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Mitosis is defined as nuclear division that produces two genetically identical daughter cells.) Tj
T*
(Prophase begins when chromosomes condense and the nuclear envelope breaks down.) Tj
T*
(During metaphase the chromosomes align along the equator of the cell.) Tj
T*
(Anaphase follows, in which sister chromatids are pulled toward opposite poles.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 43 0 R >> >> /Contents 20 0 R >>
endobj
