BT
/F1 11 Tf
56 730 Td
14 TL
(Gene Regulation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A gene is defined as a segment of DNA that encodes a functional product.) Tj
T*
(An operon is a cluster of genes transcribed together under a single promoter.) Tj
T*
(Repressor proteins bind the operator and block transcription, which switches the genes off.) Tj
T*
(Because regulation conserves energy, cells express enzymes only when the substrate is present.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 43 0 R >> >> /Contents 26 0 R >>
