BT
/F1 11 Tf
56 730 Td
14 TL
(3.5 Cellular Respiration) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Cellular respiration is defined as the process that converts glucose into usable ATP.) Tj
T*
(Glycolysis splits glucose into two molecules of pyruvate in the cytoplasm.) Tj
T*
(The citric acid cycle oxidises pyruvate derivatives and releases carbon dioxide.) Tj
T*
(Oxidative phosphorylation uses the electron transport chain to produce most of the ATP.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
27 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 43 0 R >> >> /Contents 28 0 R >>
endobj
28 0 obj
<< /Length 423 >>
stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
56 730 Td
14 TL
(Fermentation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Fermentation is defined as ATP production that proceeds without oxygen.) Tj
T*
(Lactic acid fermentation regenerates NAD+ in muscle cells during intense exercise.) Tj
T*
(Alcoholic fermentation instead produces ethanol and carbon dioxide in yeast.) Tj
T*
(Because fermentation yields far less ATP than respiration, it is used only when oxygen is scarce.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
