/F1 11 Tf
56 730 Td
14 TL
(Enzymes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(An enzyme is defined as a protein catalyst that lowers the activation energy of a reaction.) Tj
T*
(The active site is the region of the enzyme where the substrate binds.) Tj
T*
(Denaturation occurs when heat or extreme pH destroys the enzyme's three-dimensional shape.) Tj
T*
(Because shape determines function, a denatured enzyme can no longer bind its substrate.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
31 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 43 0 R >> >> /Contents 32 0 R >>
endobj
