BT
/F1 11 Tf
56 730 Td
14 TL
(Cell Communication) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A receptor is defined as a protein that binds a signalling molecule and triggers a response.) Tj
T*
(Signal transduction is the relay of a message from the receptor into the cell interior.) Tj
T*
(Second messengers such as cyclic AMP amplify the signal inside the cytoplasm.) Tj
T*
(Because amplification occurs at each step, a few molecules can produce a large response.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
