BT
/F1 11 Tf
56 730 Td
14 TL
(Homeostasis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Homeostasis is defined as the maintenance of a stable internal environment.) Tj
T*
(Negative feedback reverses a change and returns the system toward its set point.) Tj
T*
(Positive feedback amplifies a change, as occurs during blood clotting.) Tj
T*
(Because most systems must stay stable, negative feedback is far more common.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
